 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-3 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388862 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f5b753a-7fbd-50d8-93d7-41cd57d255eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388864} {:answer/id #uuid "1126107e-186e-5040-9398-edb4d6acbbee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388865} {:answer/id #uuid "387d733c-7cfe-5c37-a088-20da0dfb5afe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388866} {:answer/id #uuid "65011359-a368-5adf-95bc-7e28380bf0fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388867} {:answer/id #uuid "e576812b-f2a8-5232-87cf-c83d5c6c9f02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388868}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f5b753a-7fbd-50d8-93d7-41cd57d255eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388864} :answer-field/id #uuid "c07f5031-bde3-5457-acc7-6e1f7faa31d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388863}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4a3cbd65-d830-59dc-8511-5f72908033d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-142485" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $4\\times 5$ matrix. If $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$, find $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=5,$ and since $B$ is formed by $2$ vectors, $\\text{rank}(A)=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 2+\\text{nullity}(A) & =5 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =5-2 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-p